@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;security] native-kernel-source-provenance
Native kernel source, patch and configuration inputs MUST be fixed-output and
identified by their full immutable revision or SHA-256 digest. A rolling branch,
unhashed archive, or host compiler path MUST NOT enter a native image identity.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] native-kernel-build-fail-closed
The metadata derivation MAY produce a source/build receipt before a cross kernel
toolchain is available, but it MUST mark the kernel artifact as unavailable rather
than inventing a bootable image. Native admission remains closed until a built
kernel provides a verified byte count/digest and the matching image has recorded
boot, CID, malformed-input, reset, isolation and recovery evidence under ADR-0190.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;recovery] freebsd-static-transport-boundary
FreeBSD socket creation and bind MUST require root privilege and use the reviewed vendor family
45, guest CID 3 and peer host CID 2. Socket and queue allocations MUST remain
bounded. The static driver MUST refuse runtime detach and unload after interrupt
setup; reset and shutdown MUST fence sockets while retaining interrupt-visible
resources until VM disposal. Guest-initiated streams and hardware hot unplug MUST
NOT be claimed without separate implementation and machine evidence.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:protocol;recovery] native-peer-reset-error
A validated peer reset MUST close the matching native stream and report
ECONNRESET to the socket user. Directional shutdown MUST preserve its separate
read/write semantics instead of being treated as a transport reset.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification;security] native-booted-build-identity
Both native socket families MUST expose read-only level-AF_VSOCK option 1 as
exactly 64 lowercase hexadecimal build-input digest bytes and one NUL. Short
buffers, sets, fenced sockets and unavailable transports MUST refuse. The token
MUST bind full source, patch, configuration, build-recipe and compiler inputs independently of
the kernel file digest, and MUST NOT be called cryptographic guest attestation.
